ty) related deaths"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/2017-0090-Response-by-Surrey-County-Council_Redacted.pdf","filename":"2017-0090-Response-by-Surrey-County-Council_Redacted.pdf","promises":[],"unmatched":true}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/ronald-farrington/","title":"Ronald Farrington","date":"2017-12-22","coroner":"Caroline Topping","area":"Surrey","ref":"2017-0494","categories":["Care Home Health related deaths"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2017/12/2017-0494-Response.pdf","filename":"2017-0494-Response.pdf","promises":[{"id":784,"quote":"We have improved our systems to identify long running adult safeguarding enquiries and take actions to bring them to a satisfactory conclusion. In December 2016 15% of our adult safeguarding enquiries had been in progress for over 12 months. By December 2017 we had reduced this to 4%, despite the number of adult safeguarding enquiries we are undertaking having more than doubled over that period.","summary":"Improved systems to identify and resolve long-running safeguarding enquiries","timescale":"December 2017"}]},{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2017/12/Ronald-Farrington-Response.pdf","filename":"Ronald-Farrington-Response.pdf","promises":[{"id":1193,"quote":"we have put in place a new auditing system with close support from the local quality development team from East Surrey, this has been developed over the past year and has been met with positive feedback from the local team. The","summary":"Implement new auditing system with quality development team support","timescale":null}]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/stephen-tidey/","title":"Stephen Tidey","date":"2018-05-08","coroner":"Anna Loxton","area":"Surrey","ref":"2018-0140","categories":["Police related deaths","State Custody related deaths","Suicide (from 2015)"],"responses":[{"pdf_url"